    },
    {
      "speaker": "Dr. Elena Morris",
      "text": "And that has implications for how we report results in the lab. When we compare systems, we can’t just look at whether the extracted facts are mostly right in a qualitative sense. We have to ask whether the output is machine-consumable in exactly the expected format. A model that returns the correct entities and relations but adds an explanation at the end may appear helpful to a user, yet it fails the benchmark if the grader can’t parse the entire response as JSON."
