      "text": "That’s why our test harnesses are now built around strict schema checks and end-to-end validation. We generate sample inputs, run the extraction pipeline, and then attempt to parse the exact returned text as JSON. If parsing fails, we flag it immediately. We also check for subtle issues like trailing commas, unescaped newlines inside strings, and mismatched brackets, because any one of those can turn a potentially correct answer into a zero. In a benchmark setting, there is no partial credit for being almost right."
